From: Vitrine
Subject: [PATCH] xe: sync-only execs (no batch buffer) pass again

The single-batch check that 0001 gained on 2026-10-04 refuses
num_batch_buffer 0 as well, which Mesa's xe drivers send for execs that
only signal (Mesa 26.2: xe_queue_get_syncobj_for_idle() in
src/intel/common/xe/intel_queue.c, and ANV's is_queue_wait_idle
submissions in src/intel/vulkan/xe/anv_batch_chain.c):

- ANV, for vkQueueWaitIdle (the runtime's empty submission with one
  signal) and before destroying a queue: the refused exec sets the queue
  lost, so a Vulkan application gets VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST;
- iris, before destroying the exec queue of every GL context: refused,
  it destroys the queue without waiting, and frees buffers the GPU may
  still use.

The kernel reads `address` only for batch buffers on a parallel exec
queue (xe_exec.c: num_batch_buffer && xe_exec_queue_is_parallel()), and
takes its sync-only path for 0, so 0 needs no refusal. Vitrine's own
patch, for the research side to take over.
---
 src/drm/xe/xe_ccmd.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drm/xe/xe_ccmd.c b/src/drm/xe/xe_ccmd.c
--- a/src/drm/xe/xe_ccmd.c
+++ b/src/drm/xe/xe_ccmd.c
@@ -328,9 +328,11 @@
     * With more than one batch buffer (a parallel exec queue) the kernel
     * reads an array of addresses from the user pointer in `address`: the
     * guest's value would be a pointer into this host process.  Single-batch
-    * submissions only (all that Mesa's xe driver sends for the guest).
+    * submissions only (all that Mesa's xe driver sends for the guest), and
+    * sync-only ones: without a batch buffer the kernel does not read
+    * `address`, and Mesa sends those to wait for a queue to go idle.
     */
-   if (req->num_batch_buffer != 1) {
+   if (req->num_batch_buffer > 1) {
       drm_err("num_batch_buffer %u: only single-batch submissions",
               req->num_batch_buffer);
       rsp->ret = EINVAL;
